# app databases, JSON stores, and event logs are build artifacts of their
# readings; the readings are the source of truth (an events log with real
# history would be data, not artifact — none exists here yet). NO store.json
# is tracked, the shared ones included, and nothing reads one back. A dump is
# a materialization: reading it is reasoning about storage rather than about
# relations, which is the argument Codd 1970 opens with and the tree-shaped
# file it opens against. The store is the tables the readings project to.
*/*.db
*/*.store.json
*/*.events.jsonl
